{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/257538-fractal-as-a-cover","id":257538,"title":"Fractal as a cover","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-15T13:32:50-07:00","id":257538,"title":"Fractal as a cover","content":"No where are demon blood stated as being exempt from pacts so what if you formed a soul pact with one without being noticed? Heavy use of alibi to keep it up but it could be a way to act open as a demon well to the restrictions of a demon blood at least, with less chance of compromise with certain details.For instance no compromise for talking about demons and such while in the skin of one who would know such. You would have to ensure you only use the fractals embeds but.... It could be a way to infiltrate the machine. Target a fractal it has its eyes on and offer it a deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T15:57:54-07:00","id":257668,"title":"","content":"My gut feeling is that taking the Fractal as a Cover will erase the 'Fractal' portion of the Cover (since all Covers are Human). <br /> <br /> But my ST sense is tingling. What if a Fractal's Cipher (and most importantly it's rules) get overlaid onto the Demon's Cipher? Hmmm.... There's some story material there. I bet the G-M would love for a Demon to take a Demon-Blooded as a Cover ^.^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T17:49:08-07:00","id":257716,"title":"","content":"Ah but here is the thing, the fractal abilities doesn't have to remain. You can't see though cover as they do but by retaining the 'noted' condition or such even without benifits of it you are still monitored by the gm. So what spie theme is yet to be on the demon side? Misinformation <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T07:57:33-07:00","id":258978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/257538-fractal-as-a-cover?p=257716#post257716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah but here is the thing, the fractal abilities doesn't have to remain. You can't see though cover as they do but by retaining the 'noted' condition or such even without benifits of it you are still monitored by the gm. So what spie theme is yet to be on the demon side? Misinformation <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but at the same time as you would be Noted, there is no certainty that the Machine would pop in when you were expecting it to. So you could be in the middle of planning to dupe it, go to the agency head quarters due to being called when suddenly a half dozen hunter-angels arrive a few minutes later. You go from being a possible asset to fool the machine to being seen as a double agent by your own people. Just a thought for you to keep in mind in order to play up the drama~","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T08:00:41-07:00","id":258980,"title":"","content":"A demon who converts a supernatural gets that person as a human for their cover.<br /> <br /> I imagine the rule applies to Fractals.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Although yeah, I'd apply some of the conditions for being watched if a Fractal was along in their Cipher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T08:08:13-07:00","id":258983,"title":"","content":"Koroga, yes but that is why you'd have to make intelligent uses of alias, boltholes and other tricks so you can operate normally while still making use of such a cover. You would never walk it into your agency but have to keep it more or less always active.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T08:13:58-07:00","id":258984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/257538-fractal-as-a-cover?p=258983#post258983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Koroga, yes but that is why you'd have to make intelligent uses of alias, boltholes and other tricks so you can operate normally while still making use of such a cover. You would never walk it into your agency but have to keep it more or less always active.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but most players don't typically show that level of caution, and by proxy many demons would also slip up sooner or later. With the Demon-Blooded Cipher, it will most likely be sooner. I sort of liken it to the Plugged In Condition, though the effects of being surveyed through Noted are much more subtle, so It's all to easy to somewhat &quot;forget&quot; that you are connected- eidetic memory doesn't ensure a demon will always be aware of details, only that they can recall them if they find it prudent to do so. So yes, I think it's probably very easy to unintentionally lead the Machine to where you live and all your friends- all it takes in one busy day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 09-17-2014, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T11:47:46-07:00","id":259085,"title":"","content":"True enough. It is not something I'd suggest for long term or primary use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}